      "artist": "Dietmar Rabich",
      "description": "Office building (LVM 7 and 6) of the LVM Insurance in Münster, North Rhine-Westphalia, GermanyThe origins of today’s LVM campus date back to 1967, when the company moved into its premises on Kolde-Ring at the corner of Weseler Straße. The campus’s seven insurance buildings are located south of Münster city center. The northern part of Von-Stauffenberg-Straße runs through the campus, while Sperlichstraße forms its southern boundary. The LVM buildings were constructed between 1965 and 2014. The insurance company’s three high-rise buildings in particular are part of Münster’s skyline. The ground-level sculptures “Body and Soul” (Duk-Kyu Ryang, 2015) and “Two Horses for Münster” (Stephan Huber, 2002) are central visual elements of the site design. The 63-meter-high office tower LVM 5, known as “Crystal”, is a particularly striking building due to its design, while the 80-meter-high building LVM 3, known as “Tower”, is one of the tallest buildings in Münster.",
